{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768494-other-pure-tribes","id":768494,"title":"Other Pure Tribes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-18T07:35:41-08:00","id":768494,"title":"Other Pure Tribes","content":"Do any of the books detail (or give rumors about) other Pure Tribes besides the Ivory Claws, Predator Kings, and Fire-Touched? Alternatively, has anyone come up with any homebrew Pure Tribes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T08:02:11-08:00","id":768508,"title":"","content":"The closest you get to this in published material is that the Bale Hounds(?) are sometimes said to be patronized by a ninth wolf. <br /> <br /> Unofficially, I've debated adding two more Pure Tribes, noting that there are noticeable parallels between the existing Pure Tribes and three of the Forsaken Tribes: the Ivory Claws and the Iron Masters both show an affinity for humanity; the Predator Kings and the Hunters in Darkness both show an affinity for untamed wilderness; and the Fire-Touched and the Bone Shadows both share an affinity for the spirit world. With that in mind, I sometimes wonder what Pure counterparts to the Blood Talons and Storm Lords might look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T08:06:08-08:00","id":768510,"title":"","content":"The Ghost Wolves have a few makeshift tribes in the Rage book, and as Dataweaver pointed out the Blasphemies book offers the Bale Hounds as the Ninth Tribe. But there aren't, as far as I can tell, any other official write-ups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T10:09:13-08:00","id":768574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768494-other-pure-tribes?p=768508#post768508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest you get to this in published material is that the Bale Hounds(?) are sometimes said to be patronized by a ninth wolf.<br /> <br /> Unofficially, I've debated adding two more Pure Tribes, noting that there are noticeable parallels between the existing Pure Tribes and three of the Forsaken Tribes: the Ivory Claws and the Iron Masters both show an affinity for humanity; the Predator Kings and the Hunters in Darkness both show an affinity for untamed wilderness; and the Fire-Touched and the Bone Shadows both share an affinity for the spirit world. With that in mind, I sometimes wonder what Pure counterparts to the Blood Talons and Storm Lords might look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's parallels with the Predator Kings and Blood Talons, the Fire-Touched and Hunters in Darkness, and the Ivory Claws and Storm Lords as well that you probably missed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T16:13:43-08:00","id":768772,"title":"","content":"I just love Bale Hounds as <b>secret</b> Tribe that is inside all others 8 and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\">worshiping what have left of Wolf</a>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:48:14-08:00","id":769942,"title":"","content":"I personally have made a home brew tribe that is more of a dark mirror of the Iron Masters in their adaptive nature and preying upon human kind, though for 2nd Ed they do have to be re worked due to the Ivory Claws getting more focus on the human manipulating rivalry with the Iron Masters. But I do like the idea of a Pure Tribe that is more warrior based, the Predator Kings are a good rival for the Blood Talons yeah, but they are very much more Hunters in Darkness and Bone Shadow like in terms of their tribes goals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:50:00-08:00","id":769944,"title":"","content":"Could you tell us more about these Iron Masters of the Pure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T07:39:22-08:00","id":769975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768494-other-pure-tribes?p=769944#post769944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you tell us more about these Iron Masters of the Pure?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright. They are known as the Fang-Shapers, a tribe that once followed the Firstborn Danu-Ur( a separate spirit from Rabid Wolf in my setting), and when Father Wolf was killed, her grief and rage changed her nature subtly, but it was enough to make her appearance become radically different, her steely pelt became engulfed in flames, her name changing from Creator Wolf to Burning Wolf. She was still a spirit of creation, but creation now aimed towards destructive ends. She attempted to personally kill the traitorous pups that would form the forsaken, but Red Wolf and Destroyer Wolf intervened and killed her, albeit unintentionally. The Uratha who were spared by her would be nearly destroyed by the Forsaken generations after Her death, though an unlikely spirit came to their aid. For despite Urfarah's wishes, she had once mated with another wolf spirit and bore a cub in secret, a Secondborn named Smoldering Wolf. This cub was equally angry with the Forsaken, as like the innocent Uratha he had also lost both his Mother and Grandfather. This spirit would then become their Totem, and they would become a tribe who were Pure, though they wouldn't be accepted as Pure until millenia later, during the later years of Rome-that was when Smoldering Wolf was powerful enough to be on part with the Firstborn in terms of spiritual strength- though only just barely.<br /> <br /> As a tribe, they pretty much were fetish makers and spirit trappers, they essentially were a &quot;Logistical&quot; tribe due to their youth and Smoldering Wolf's nature. They believed that to be truly apex predators above humans and the forsaken, their teeth needed to be longer and sharper, so they have adapted by mimicking what makes humans so dangerous when they are so weak compared to other creatures; invention and weaponry. It was actually far more complex than that, but I don't have the time to go make a whole thread to explain them at this time. Suffice it to say, they were pretty much a fusion of 2nd Ed Fire-Touched and Ivory Claws in how they operated, which is why I am reworking them immensely lol. I probably will have them secretly in thrall with an Idigam, due to their big schtick was the ability to manipulate spirit matter in a way eerily similar to Essence Shaping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 11-20-2015, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}